    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDYwODEyNmE1MjFkYmYyNWI4ZjQwZWY1NjdlNDkxODg5ZjUyOWVhZGI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T03:33:05Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T03:33:05Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(adaptive): close the entry orbit exactly on its start\n\nThe HSM plan orbits the entry from its start and leaves the orbit where\nit closed. adaptive::rings::circle computed the closing vertex at\na0 + TAU, an ulp off the start, and the plan's crossing law (orientation\npredicate) read the spiral's first chord out of it as a proper crossing\nof the orbit's first chord: the level was refused and cut with Offset\nrings. That is why the user's STEP bore lost its HSM plan on Z 20 (since\n#850) and Z 10 (since #839's finer mesh reshuffled the float noise).\n\nThe circle now closes exactly - its last point is its first, and the\nstart itself where the start lies on the circle (within 1e-9 mm). The\ncrossing law is unchanged.\n\nPinned by motion adaptive_orbit_seam (the dumped Z 10 center outline as\na 2-D pocket; crossed before the fix) and a rings unit test; the heavy\napp pin is re-measured: no level falls back, 16197 / 15458 / 1581.\n\nFixes #980\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
